{
  "name": "Unraid · Sysadmin & Telegram bot",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Unraid · Sysadmin & Telegram bot\nThe **only** workflow with a Telegram Trigger (a bot delivers updates to a single webhook). It answers sysadmin commands itself and forwards Docker commands to the *Docker updates & actions* workflow.\n\n**Sysadmin:** /status · /info · /disks · /parity · /parity_start · /parity_pause · /parity_resume · /parity_cancel · /syslog · /notifications · /archive_all · /vms · /help\n**Docker:** /containers · /updates · /update_all · /update_<name> · /restart_<name> · /start_<name> · /stop_<name> · /logs_<name>\n\nOnly chats listed in **cfg.allowedChatIds** are served. Until it is set, the bot only replies with the sender's chat ID, so you can find yours and nothing else runs.",
        "width": 640,
        "height": 420
      },
      "id": "4a76cfa6-155e-4383-a1a5-1441babac799",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -460
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup\n1. Create a bot with **@BotFather**, add a **Telegram** credential with its token, and select it in the trigger and both Telegram nodes.\n2. Select the **Unraid API** credential in the Unraid nodes.\n3. Publish / activate, send the bot any message: it replies with your chat ID. Put it in **Bot settings › cfg.allowedChatIds** (comma-separated for several) and in the other two workflows' settings.\n4. In **Run Docker workflow** pick the *Unraid · Docker updates & actions* workflow (publish that one too).\n5. Optional: send BotFather /setcommands with the list in the README so commands autocomplete.",
        "width": 560,
        "height": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "1eb6d1fc-408d-4148-a831-ffdb725362d9",
      "name": "Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -340,
        -460
      ]
    },
